From precice-ohos-adapt <precice-ohos-adapt@users.noreply.gitcode.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Conan Boost mapping: Boost::boost -> Boost::headers

Conan CMakeDeps for boost/1.91.0.1.3 publishes component targets
Boost::headers / Boost::log / Boost::thread / ... but no umbrella
Boost::boost target (official Boost CMake provides it). Upstream
preciceCore links the umbrella for header-only includes, which fails
the generate step with "Target preciceCore links to Boost::boost but
the target was not found". Map the umbrella to the Conan header-only
component; compiled Boost libs stay on their explicit targets.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -429,7 +429,7 @@
 # Setup Boost
 target_compile_definitions(preciceCore PUBLIC BOOST_ALL_DYN_LINK BOOST_ASIO_ENABLE_OLD_SERVICES BOOST_GEOMETRY_DISABLE_DEPRECATED_03_WARNING)
 target_link_libraries(preciceCore PUBLIC
-  Boost::boost
+  Boost::headers
   Boost::log
   Boost::log_setup
   Boost::program_options
